## keygraphjs Changelog


Current WIP
-----------

- **in-app confirmation dialog** replaces the browser-native `confirm()` for the
  destructive actions (like "New complete graph"). The
  new dialog is a small modal styled like the rest of the UI (Enter confirms,
  Escape cancels, focus is trapped inside while open)
- new **"Example graphs…"** toolbar dropdown with well-known preset graphs.
  The undirected ones: Two Hubs, Petersen, K3,3, Krackhardt kite, hypercube Q3,
  star (S8), cycle (C8), binary tree, 4×4 grid. A **Directed** section adds:
  DAG, Dijkstra's weighted shortest-path graph (CLRS Fig 24.6), the strongly-
  connected-components graph (CLRS Fig 22.9, includes a self-loop), a max-flow
  network (CLRS Fig 26.1), a regular tournament (T5), and the binary de Bruijn
  graph B(2,2) (includes two self-loops). Each directed example switches the
  app into directed mode
- the startup sample graph is renamed to **"Two Hubs"** (was "A/B hub example")
  and is now also reachable from the Example graphs menu
- Add support for edges / vertex weights in arbitrary range, no longer limited
  to [0, 1]
- Add number input for precise weight value input (in addition to sliders)

v0.2.0 -- Directed graph support
----------------------------------

New feature: support for **directed graphs** (in addition to undirected ones).

- global **directed/undirected mode** with a toolbar toggle (`Mode: …`); the mode
  is stored in the JSON (`"directed": true`) and shown in the stats line
- destructive actions ask for confirmation: switching the graph mode, and
  **"New complete graph"** (which replaces the current graph)
- conversion rules: undirected → directed doubles the edge count (each edge
  becomes two directed edges, weights copied); directed → undirected merges a
  bidirectional pair into one edge using the **mean** weight (a lone directed
  edge is kept as-is)
- directed edges are drawn with **arrow tips**; a bidirectional pair (A→B and B→A)
  renders as a **single line with an arrowhead at both ends** (no second curve)
- per-direction edge **weights**; on the canvas a pair's label shows both numbers
  ("0.90 | 0.30"; first = lower-id → higher-id), the tooltip lists both directions
- "Add node → fully connected" adds edges in **both directions** in directed mode;
  "Connect nodes" treats A→B and B→A as distinct edges; right-clicking a collapsed
  pair deletes **both** directions (use the list to delete a single direction)
- import/export: GML `directed 1/0`, GraphML `edgedefault=`, DOT `digraph` / `->`;
  mixed graphs (per-edge overrides of the graph default) are rejected on import
- accessibility: accessible names (`aria-label`) for the weight sliders, icon
  buttons and checkboxes; the status message is a live region (polite, assertive
  for errors); the graph canvas has an accessible label synced with the stats;
  the Export…/Add node dropdown buttons expose `aria-expanded`
- autosave: the current graph (nodes, edges, weights, layout positions, mode) is
  silently saved to localStorage (debounced 500 ms) and restored on the next
  visit — a refresh, tab close or crash no longer loses work; falls back to
  sessionStorage when localStorage is unavailable
- new "Vertex weights" toggle (View toolbar): shows each node's weight value
  below its name on the canvas, mirroring the existing edge-label toggle
- removed the "Delete selected edge" toolbar button — deleting an edge is done
  via the right-click context menu or the sidebar ✕ (the button was redundant,
  asymmetric with nodes, and could delete all incident edges when a node was
  selected, since clicking a node selects its edges)

v0.1.0 -- Initial release
--------------------------

Most relevant features:

- display and edit undirected graphs, option for edge weights and vertex weights
- drag nodes and run a one-shot force-directed **auto-layout** (with undo)
- add and remove nodes, and connect nodes to add edges
- edit edge **weights** (0–1) per edge, or select several and set them all at once
- set a **node weight** (0–1) per node — heavier nodes draw larger and export with the weight
- give nodes human-readable **names** and arbitrary **groups** (colors are assigned automatically)
- toggle edge-weight labels in the view
- **load and save** graphs in JSON or standard formats (GML, GraphML)
